    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 5 USER]\ne039\tWe learned today that installation is easier than we thought for people using the common package manager, but one private lab had a staff engineer quietly solving problems for everyone.\ne040\tTheir researchers reported a smooth experience because they never saw the setup work.\ne041\tThat makes our private evidence look weaker.\ne042\tOn the other hand, a volunteer wrote a new installer over the weekend and wants real users before polishing it.\ne043\tI cannot tell whether this argues for release or for another round of testing.\n[Turn 5 ASSISTANT]\ne044\tIt argues against treating the private labs as representative, but it does not choose the next step by itself.\ne045\tThe new installer could change the support burden, and public use could test it under real conditions.\ne046\tA bounded installation test with people who lack staff engineering might answer that question faster than either a full beta or more internal polishing.\ne047\tStill, if every uncertainty becomes a separate pre-release study, you recreate the endless preview problem you already identified.",
